# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# service-video-mesh-edge — minimum required configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the four values below. Everything else
# has sane defaults; you only need to override them if your network
# situation is unusual (NAT-with-port-translation, IPv6-only, etc).
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public DNS name of THIS edge host. Must resolve to this machine's
# public IPv4. Caddy uses it for LE cert provisioning; moq-relay binds
# its TLS cert against it; the edge node advertises it to the leader
# so /v1/assign can route viewers here.
#
# Examples:
#   edge1.example.com
#   159-223-116-200.nip.io      (free wildcard DNS for any public IP)
EDGE_HOSTNAME=

# HTTPS URL of the mesh leader you want to attach to. The edge fetches
# verify keys from <LEADER_URL>/v1/jwks, opens a WSS to /mesh for the
# enrollment handshake, and receives a fresh cluster JWT in the
# response.
#
# Example: https://mesh.example.com
LEADER_URL=

# Email Let's Encrypt sends expiry/renewal notices to.
CADDY_ACME_EMAIL=

# (optional but recommended) Leader's Ed25519 pubkey, base64. Pinning
# this defends against a MITM on first contact: the edge refuses to
# enroll if the leader returns a different pubkey. Fetch via:
#   curl -s $LEADER_URL/v1/version | jq -r .leaderPubkey
LEADER_PUBKEY=

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Tune only if you know why.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where viewer-receipt payouts should flow. If unset the leader pays
# itself for traffic this edge serves — fine for a hobbyist edge, less
# fine if you want to be compensated for the bandwidth you provide.
# EVM 0x-address, lower- or mixed-case.
# EDGE_PAYOUT_ADDRESS=

# Concurrent viewer ceiling. The leader's selector won't route more
# than this many viewers to you at once. Conservative default below;
# raise once you've seen the box keep up.
EDGE_MAX_CONSUMERS=500

# Outbound bandwidth cap (bytes/sec). 0 = no cap; the leader still
# routes based on count. Setting this lets the selector apply
# backpressure before you saturate.
# Example: 100 Mbps = 12500000
EDGE_MAX_EGRESS_BPS=0

# Override the published mesh-edge image. Default pulls latest from
# the upstream registry; pin to a SHA tag for reproducible deploys.
# EDGE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/bozp-pzob/service-video-mesh-edge:sha-abc1234

# Override the locally-built moq-relay image tag. Default builds from
# the bundled Dockerfile.moq-relay on first `docker compose up`.
# MOQ_RELAY_IMAGE=mesh-moq-relay:local
